  {
    "doc_id": "DOC-RUNBOOK-006",
    "title": "Enterprise Credential Rotation & Emergency Revocation Runbook",
    "category": "Security Policy",
    "clearance_level": 3,
    "metadata": {
      "environment": "production",
      "owner": "security-team",
      "tags": [
        "runbook",
        "rotation",
        "incident-response",
        "security"
      ]
    },
    "content": "# Enterprise Secret Rotation & Emergency Revocation Protocol\n\n### Standard 90-Day Rotation Schedule\n1. Generate a new high-entropy 256-bit token or asymmetric cryptographic keypair.\n2. Ingest the updated secret into Sovereign Vault under label `next-generation`.\n3. Conduct zero-downtime rolling restart of microservices.\n4. Validate monitoring metrics on Grafana before deprecating legacy tokens.\n\n### Emergency Incident Revocation\nIf credential compromise is suspected:\n- Execute: `python -m vault.cli --revoke-token <TOKEN_ID> --broadcast-all`\n- Apply immediate IAM quarantine: `aws iam attach-user-policy --policy-arn arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AWSDenyAll --user-name <USER>`."
  },
